WEBVTT

1
00:01:01.291 --> 00:01:04.416
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna explained</b>

2
00:01:04.416 --> 00:01:10.375
<b>that a person who enjoys the gifts of life and the facilities received from it,</b>

3
00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:14.583
<b>but does not offer anything to the deities in return</b>

4
00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:17.291
<b>or perform any kind of sacrifice,</b>

5
00:01:17.291 --> 00:01:21.708
<b>will certainly be considered a thief.</b>

6
00:01:21.708 --> 00:01:29.000
<b>Now, Krishna is discussing how</b>
<b>a seemingly simple act</b>

7
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:39.750
<b>like eating can bind us to the bondage of karma, </b>
<b>i.e., the bondage of sin and virtue,</b>

8
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:43.708
<b>and how a person can free themselves </b>
<b>from this bondage.</b>

9
00:01:43.708 --> 00:01:48.958
<b>Through these discussions, Krishna is </b>
<b>also refuting Arjuna's misconceptions.</b>

10
00:01:48.958 --> 00:01:51.000
<b>Arjuna had expressed his desire</b>

11
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:57.416
<b>to live a life of begging rather than </b>
<b>enjoy the kingdom obtained through war.</b>

12
00:01:57.416 --> 00:02:01.083
<b>At least, in that case, he would not </b>
<b>be committing any sin.</b>

13
00:02:01.083 --> 00:02:04.208
<b>These verses also refute that notion.</b>

14
00:02:04.208 --> 00:02:06.541
<b>Even if one lives like a beggar</b>

15
00:02:06.541 --> 00:02:08.833
<b>or consumes simple food,</b>

16
00:02:08.833 --> 00:02:12.333
<b>the bondage of sin and virtue still exists.</b>

17
00:02:12.333 --> 00:02:16.291
<b>Let us understand this in these verses.</b>

18
00:02:21.125 --> 00:02:22.916
<b>Lord Krishna says</b>

19
00:02:22.916 --> 00:02:28.083
<b>that when food is offered in </b>
<b>a sacrifice before consuming it,</b>

20
00:02:28.083 --> 00:02:31.250
<b>and the deities are offered their share,</b>

21
00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:35.416
<b>then that food becomes free from all sins.</b>

22
00:02:35.416 --> 00:02:36.125
<b>But</b>

23
00:02:36.125 --> 00:02:42.083
<b>a person who does not do this and </b>
<b>eats only for their personal satisfaction</b>

24
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:44.875
<b>becomes a partaker of sin.</b>

25
00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:46.333
<b>But why is this so?</b>

26
00:02:46.333 --> 00:02:50.125
<b>This question must have </b>
<b>certainly arisen in your mind.</b>

27
00:02:50.125 --> 00:02:51.583
<b>According to the Vedas,</b>

28
00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:54.500
<b>consuming meat is indeed a sin.</b>

29
00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:55.666
<b>You tell me,</b>

30
00:02:55.666 --> 00:03:02.958
<b>if someone kills an animal </b>
<b>for the taste of their tongue</b>

31
00:03:02.958 --> 00:03:05.083
<b>or to fill their stomach, would it not be a sin?</b>

32
00:03:05.083 --> 00:03:07.750
<b>But this is about non-vegetarian food.</b>

33
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:11.583
<b>Even in vegetarian food, plants are cut,</b>

34
00:03:11.583 --> 00:03:13.916
<b>roots are uprooted,</b>

35
00:03:13.916 --> 00:03:15.625
<b>there is pain here too,</b>

36
00:03:15.625 --> 00:03:17.708
<b>there is bondage of karma here too.</b>

37
00:03:17.708 --> 00:03:21.041
<b>Therefore, even if the food is vegetarian,</b>

38
00:03:21.041 --> 00:03:23.750
<b>it is necessary that before consuming it,</b>

39
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:29.500
<b>it should be offered to the deities or </b>
<b>to the Supreme Lord Vishnu,</b>

40
00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.333
<b>and then taken as prasad.</b>

41
00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:35.250
<b>Krishna also explains</b>

42
00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.833
<b>that all living beings depend on food grains,</b>

43
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:42.083
<b>the production of which requires rain,</b>

44
00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:44.875
<b>and rain is produced from yajna (sacrifice).</b>

45
00:03:44.875 --> 00:03:50.125
<b>And yajna happens only when a </b>
<b>person fulfills their prescribed duties.</b>

46
00:03:50.125 --> 00:03:51.000
<b>That means,</b>

47
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:57.291
<b>even to merely stay alive, a person </b>
<b>must perform their duties.</b>

48
00:03:57.291 --> 00:04:01.083
<b>These duties of humans are </b>
<b>based on the Vedic scriptures</b>

49
00:04:01.083 --> 00:04:04.125
<b>created by Lord Vishnu.</b>

50
00:04:04.125 --> 00:04:05.000
<b>That means,</b>

51
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:10.541
<b>Lord Vishnu Himself is inherent in </b>
<b>every sacrifice in the form of human duties.</b>

52
00:04:10.541 --> 00:04:15.041
<b>Thus, even a person unaware</b>
<b>of Lord Vishnu's presence</b>

53
00:04:15.041 --> 00:04:18.125
<b>cannot remain independent of Him.</b>

54
00:04:18.125 --> 00:04:20.166
<b>This awareness is necessary</b>

55
00:04:20.166 --> 00:04:24.166
<b>because it leads a person towards Lord Vishnu.</b>

56
00:04:24.166 --> 00:04:28.458
<b>Offering food to Lord Vishnu before eating,</b>

57
00:04:28.458 --> 00:04:31.333
<b>then accepting it as His prasad,</b>

58
00:04:31.333 --> 00:04:36.041
<b>is the beginning of the path to reach Lord Vishnu.</b>

59
00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:45.208
<b>Humans desire freedom from </b>
<b>the bondage of karma,</b>

60
00:04:45.208 --> 00:04:50.958
<b>but they do not properly </b>
<b>understand this bondage.</b>

61
00:04:50.958 --> 00:04:57.250
<b>In your personal life, every object you enjoy or use</b>

62
00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:04.250
<b>has a moral impact on your life and karmic ties, </b>

63
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.916
<b>even if it's a daily activity like eating.</b>

64
00:05:08.916 --> 00:05:16.000
<b>In diet, vegetarianism is certainly far better </b>
<b>than killing animals and consuming meat.</b>

65
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.833
<b>However,</b>

66
00:05:17.833 --> 00:05:21.500
<b>to be free from the karmic bonds of food,</b>

67
00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:25.708
<b>certain additional practices are necessary </b>
<b>along with a vegetarian diet.</b>

68
00:05:25.708 --> 00:05:26.666
<b>First,</b>

69
00:05:26.666 --> 00:05:32.583
<b>cultivate a sense of gratitude for the food you eat</b>

70
00:05:32.583 --> 00:05:38.625
<b>and recognize the invisible efforts of many</b>
<b>individuals involved in it.</b>

71
00:05:38.625 --> 00:05:42.250
<b>Respect the farmers who grow it,</b>

72
00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:49.208
<b>the laborers who carefully harvest and sort it,</b>

73
00:05:49.208 --> 00:05:58.083
<b>as well as those who systematically collect it and </b>
<b>deliver it to you through the market.</b>

74
00:05:58.083 --> 00:06:01.750
<b>Express gratitude to all of them.</b>

75
00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.416
<b>Then,</b>

76
00:06:03.416 --> 00:06:11.500
<b>incorporate the process of offering the food to </b>
<b>God before eating it into your daily routine.</b>

77
00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:16.375
<b>This practice will purify your mind and soul,</b>

78
00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:21.208
<b>keeping you free from the karmic bonds</b>
<b>associated with that food.</b>

79
00:06:21.208 --> 00:06:25.375
<b>Every particle of food is blessed by God,</b>

80
00:06:25.375 --> 00:06:28.416
<b>each particle is His prasad.</b>

81
00:06:28.416 --> 00:06:31.625
<b>This thought will increase humility in you</b>

82
00:06:31.625 --> 00:06:37.791
<b>and also inspire you to view this world</b>
<b>from a spiritual perspective.</b>

83
00:06:37.791 --> 00:06:44.375
<b>This awareness about all beings, plants, etc, </b>
<b>of the world</b>

84
00:06:44.375 --> 00:06:47.750
<b>will help you understand the interdependence.</b>

85
00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.083
<b>And</b>

86
00:06:49.083 --> 00:06:52.041
<b>you will also begin to understand</b>

87
00:06:52.041 --> 00:06:56.541
<b>how this creation depends on divine grace.</b>

88
00:06:56.541 --> 00:07:03.666
<b>This very mindset will help lead you </b>
<b>to higher spiritual goals.</b>

89
00:07:03.666 --> 00:07:05.208
<b>Think about it.</b>

90
00:07:09.541 --> 00:07:16.541
<b>There are many food-related traditions in</b>
<b>society that are still prevalent today.</b>

91
00:07:16.541 --> 00:07:18.208
<b>For example,</b>

92
00:07:18.208 --> 00:07:24.291
<b>in many homes, the cooked food </b>
<b>is first offered to God.</b>

93
00:07:24.291 --> 00:07:29.666
<b>Some people dedicate a portion </b>
<b>of the food to the holy cow,</b>

94
00:07:29.666 --> 00:07:30.333
<b>or</b>

95
00:07:30.333 --> 00:07:32.958
<b>it is offered into the sacred fire.</b>

96
00:07:32.958 --> 00:07:37.583
<b>The core purpose behind all these is the same –</b>

97
00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:45.958
<b>to express gratitude and appreciation for</b>
<b>the food that nourishes our bodies.</b>

98
00:07:45.958 --> 00:07:53.416
<b>These beliefs are not only spiritual </b>
<b>but also have practical benefits.</b>

99
00:07:53.416 --> 00:08:01.541
<b>If you give so much respect to food, </b>
<b>consider it as prasad, will you waste it?</b>

100
00:08:01.541 --> 00:08:03.416
<b>Consider this,</b>

101
00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:09.333
<b>if even a small percentage of people </b>
<b>on Earth start this practice,</b>

102
00:08:09.333 --> 00:08:12.958
<b>how much food will be saved from going to waste.</b>

103
00:08:12.958 --> 00:08:17.083
<b>Perhaps then no one will go hungry.</b>

104
00:08:17.083 --> 00:08:23.500
<b>This food is a gift of this very creation, </b>
<b>no one owns it.</b>

105
00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:29.083
<b>How beautiful is the thought of looking </b>
<b>at food from a spiritual perspective,</b>

106
00:08:29.083 --> 00:08:34.041
<b>respecting it, not wasting it,</b>

107
00:08:34.041 --> 00:08:39.333
<b>and as a result, no person ever remaining hungry.</b>

108
00:08:39.333 --> 00:08:45.083
<b>Any big initiative begins with small steps.</b>

109
00:08:45.083 --> 00:08:49.125
<b>Start with your family.</b>

110
00:08:49.125 --> 00:08:53.833
<b>Always maintain respect for food, </b>
<b>express gratitude</b>

111
00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:57.791
<b>to that Lord who created this universe,</b>

112
00:08:57.791 --> 00:08:59.166
<b>created food,</b>

113
00:08:59.166 --> 00:09:05.416
<b>be grateful to all those who brought it to you.</b>

114
00:09:05.416 --> 00:09:10.000
<b>By doing so, not only will the food </b>
<b>provide more satisfaction,</b>

115
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:14.250
<b>but happiness will also arise in the mind.</b>

116
00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:16.083
<b>Think about it.</b>

117
00:09:20.375 --> 00:09:25.250
<b>Everything in creation is dependent </b>
<b>on interdependence.</b>

118
00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:30.166
<b>The farmer sowing the seed, the </b>
<b>seed germinating from the rain,</b>

119
00:09:30.166 --> 00:09:34.291
<b>the nourishment of that </b>
<b>germinated seed from the sun and air,</b>

120
00:09:34.291 --> 00:09:38.500
<b>the cultivation of that field with </b>
<b>a plow made by someone else.</b>

121
00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:44.416
<b>That same grain and vegetable is then </b>
<b>cooked by someone on fire.</b>

122
00:09:44.416 --> 00:09:47.791
<b>The delicious dish you enjoy</b>

123
00:09:47.791 --> 00:09:52.916
<b>has the hand of countless people</b>
<b>and elements behind it.</b>

124
00:09:52.916 --> 00:09:55.833
<b>But the beautiful thing is that </b>

125
00:09:55.833 --> 00:09:59.458
<b>the dish you enjoyed</b>

126
00:09:59.458 --> 00:10:02.708
<b>was not consumed by the farmer,</b>

127
00:10:02.708 --> 00:10:09.791
<b>nor by the rain, sun, air, or fire.</b>

128
00:10:09.791 --> 00:10:12.333
<b>Everyone did their karma,</b>

129
00:10:12.333 --> 00:10:16.583
<b>the purpose of which was to </b>
<b>satiate your stomach,</b>

130
00:10:16.583 --> 00:10:20.166
<b> to gratify your tongue.</b>

131
00:10:20.166 --> 00:10:26.875
<b>What a beautiful example of cooperation </b>
<b>and interdependence for a common goal this is.</b>

132
00:10:26.875 --> 00:10:30.250
<b>Professional life is also like this.</b>

133
00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:37.125
<b>The success of any business involves the </b>
<b>contribution of many people and several factors.</b>

134
00:10:37.125 --> 00:10:38.458
<b>It is necessary</b>

135
00:10:38.458 --> 00:10:43.875
<b>that all the people working in </b>
<b>that business give their best effort,</b>

136
00:10:43.875 --> 00:10:46.291
<b>cooperate with each other,</b>

137
00:10:46.291 --> 00:10:50.166
<b>and together lead that organization to success.</b>

138
00:10:50.166 --> 00:10:53.875
<b>The fruit of the organization's success</b>
<b>will come to you,</b>

139
00:10:53.875 --> 00:10:59.250
<b>and no effort goes in vain,</b>

140
00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:04.000
<b>it also strengthens you for the future.</b>

141
00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.541
<b>Therefore,</b>

142
00:11:05.541 --> 00:11:07.833
<b>for personal success too,</b>

143
00:11:07.833 --> 00:11:10.958
<b>diligently fulfill your duties through hard work,</b>

144
00:11:10.958 --> 00:11:13.833
<b>and definitely cooperate with others as well.</b>

145
00:11:13.833 --> 00:11:14.791
<b>But</b>

146
00:11:14.791 --> 00:11:19.208
<b>if you become selfish in this journey,</b>

147
00:11:19.208 --> 00:11:25.375
<b>then ultimately you will achieve neither </b>
<b>collective success nor personal success.</b>

148
00:11:25.375 --> 00:11:33.458
<b>It is important that you help others yourself </b>
<b>and be grateful for the help of others.</b>

149
00:11:33.458 --> 00:11:34.875
<b>Otherwise,</b>

150
00:11:34.875 --> 00:11:41.916
<b>just as eating done only for personal satiation </b>
<b>without expressing gratitude</b>

151
00:11:41.916 --> 00:11:45.583
<b>makes one a partaker of bad karma,</b>

152
00:11:45.583 --> 00:11:47.291
<b>Similarly,</b>

153
00:11:47.291 --> 00:11:53.541
<b>success tainted with selfishness will also lead </b>
<b>you towards the bondage of sin.</b>

